			<div class="forum_comment_action_menu" style="display: none;" id="forum_comment_actions_menu_567049339876416999">				<a class="forum_comment_action report tooltip" href="javascript:Forum_ShowReportDialog( '103582791475792396', '591813437999456887', '569300439979438766', '407616740', '567049339876416999' );" data-tooltip-text="Report this post for inappropriate content.  Reported post are flagged for review by moderators.">
				<span class="non_breaking_space">&nbsp;</span><img src="https://community.fastly.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/notification_icon_flag_dark.png?v=1">Report this post</a>
			</div>
							</div>
			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_567049339876416999">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c567049339876413534">spitfire_ch</a></b>:</div>I'm also just curious: why is it OK for programming but not for art? I'm actually a SQL developer (Data Analyst/Engineer), and my job is as much at stake as an artist's — probably even more so. I try to embrace AI as much as possible to avoid being left behind. In my opinion, it's OK to use AI for programming and everything else. Unless you use the environment argument, in which case it's not OK for anything, and I am very much guilty myself. But I don't get why artists always are the big victims in the AI world. </blockquote><br>I'm a video game student in a game design school at Isart digital Paris. In this school we also have game artists and sound designers that have huge difficulties to find jobs, because of the current situation of the video game industry. Generated art from AI is mainly art stole from artists that never wanted this tool. So for that main reason I prefere pay commercial license of real artist (like I did for the artwork of the inspector Reye, for the sound, it's a free licence). <br><br>But for the programmation, AI created more jobs than it deleted them (In France at least). Secondly, depending on how you use it, programming don't remove the creative part of making a game. <br><br>For the translation, i'm a bit frustated to use AI, but I prefere that than don't translate anything. For now i didn't received any money so I can't afford for translation compagny, but maybe after the release I will contact it to arrange that part of the game.			</div>
			<div class="comment_footer_ctn">
													
				
