			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_567049339876418855">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c567049339876413534">spitfire_ch</a></b>:</div>I'm also just curious: why is it OK for programming but not for art? I'm actually a SQL developer (Data Analyst/Engineer), and my job is as much at stake as an artist's — probably even more so. I try to embrace AI as much as possible to avoid being left behind. In my opinion, it's OK to use AI for programming and everything else. Unless you use the environment argument, in which case it's not OK for anything, and I am very much guilty myself. But I don't get why artists always are the big victims in the AI world. </blockquote><br><br>First of all just look how easy and effortless is to make something with AI. Anyone who never touch the pencil in his life can create digital art now wihtout talent, work or effort. Why to pay for it? What value it has. Secondly art is the thing we see in game and interact with, code is like backend. Of course i'm against AI in all aspects of game  creation.			</div>
