				<div class="commentthread_comment_actions" >
														<a class="forum_comment_action forum_comment_action_trigger" data-tooltip-type="selector" data-tooltip-content="#forum_comment_actions_menu_562546073917426117">
					<span><i class="ico16 arrow_down"></i></span>
				</a>
			
			<div class="forum_comment_action_menu" style="display: none;" id="forum_comment_actions_menu_562546073917426117">				<a class="forum_comment_action report tooltip" href="javascript:Forum_ShowReportDialog( '103582791475792396', '591813437999456887', '569300439979438766', '10463251', '562546073917426117' );" data-tooltip-text="Report this post for inappropriate content.  Reported post are flagged for review by moderators.">
				<span class="non_breaking_space">&nbsp;</span><img src="https://community.fastly.steamstatic.com/public/images/skin_1/notification_icon_flag_dark.png?v=1">Report this post</a>
			</div>
							</div>
			</div>
			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_562546073917426117">
				AI creates images from scratch by learning mathematical patterns and concepts, exactly the same way it generates code or text. It doesn't copy or store source images—it uses them as learning material, much like a human artist studies the work of others to build their own style.			</div>
