				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c567049339876413534">spitfire_ch</a></b>:</div>I'm also just curious: why is it OK for programming but not for art? I'm actually a SQL developer (Data Analyst/Engineer), and my job is as much at stake as an artist's — probably even more so. I try to embrace AI as much as possible to avoid being left behind. In my opinion, it's OK to use AI for programming and everything else. Unless you use the environment argument, in which case it's not OK for anything, and I am very much guilty myself. But I don't get why artists always are the big victims in the AI world. </blockquote>I don't think this developer was ever going to hire you so you don't have to worry about that.			</div>
