			<div class="commentthread_comment_text" id="comment_content_562546073917526540">
				<blockquote class="bb_blockquote with_author"><div class="bb_quoteauthor">Originally posted by <b><a href="#c567049623178320125">nomadredd</a></b>:</div>Are gamers/people dont like AI?  I do professional SQL development and we use AI for queries now too.    AI is just the way to go these days, more productive.   Though the modelling and business analyst part of the work still requires real humans to think and validate.    <br><br>I have used AI much in the development and it's just a tool like a calculator.  At the end of the day, one's work speaks for itself if it is good or slop, regardless if it was doing 100% by people or not. </blockquote>That guy said &quot; Unless you use the environment argument, in which case it's not OK for anything, and I am very much guilty myself.&quot; Idk wtf that means but whoever hired him should def replace him with an AI. you're right that actual analysis and system architecting should secure your job.			</div>
			<div class="comment_footer_ctn">
